From a494b87925f2e877e1c5e2466c1211a35f12a758 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeltaTor <deltator@example.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:54:36 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] conflux: add ConfluxSetSelection 6, hybrid warm-up then
 fastest set

Add a hybrid set-selection policy: behave exactly like mode 4 while the pool is
still being measured, then behave exactly like mode 5 once it has been measured.

Phase 1 (warm-up) is the existing weighted spread with its 10% floor, so every
set keeps getting real traffic and is measured, and ConfluxProbeWarmupInterval
still refreshes the weights from the cumulative bytes and active time since the
window opened, so the connection is already fast while the estimate is young.
Phase 2 (exploit) sends every new stream only to the highest measured
throughput, with no floor, exactly like mode 5.

The phase boundary is tracked per set with mthr_measured_once, set when a set
completes its first full measurement window. The hybrid policy stays in phase 1
while any candidate has not been measured yet and switches to phase 2 once all
of them have, which is normally one ConfluxProbeInterval after the sets appear.
A rebuilt set is a fresh conflux_t and starts unmeasured, so it re-warms the
pool instead of leaving an unmeasured set out of the comparison.

The measured-throughput branches of conflux_pick_set_from_candidates are also
consolidated into shared weighted/exploit helpers, so modes 4, 5 and 6 differ
only in the phase decision. ConfluxSetSelection now accepts 0-6; the default is
still 1 and the shipped configs stay on 4.
